From 234fb4f3b4a55e3660fccee48df1daf25045170d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (developer)" <dev@meetfa.local>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 18:38:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test(sw): replace sleep-based settling with deterministic
 queue drain

Root causes of intermittent Service Worker test failures:
1. Tests waited a fixed settle(60ms) for the SW serial queue; under cold
   start / parallel workers on a loaded CPU the queue (~20-30ms idle)
   was still mid-processing (observed: active, segmentCount 0).
2. 'different meet code' asserted list order, but both sessions can share
   the same startedAt millisecond; tie order is undefined (random UUID key).

Changes:
- serviceWorker.ts: export whenIdle() (awaits existing chain; no behavior change)
- tests: await sw.whenIdle() instead of sleeps; fake setTimeout for the
  LIVE_PERSIST_MS boundary; SW restart clears old listeners
- regression: slow storage (150ms) proves fixed sleep is insufficient and
  whenIdle is; whenIdle covers work enqueued while waiting; same-ms sessions
- README: test count 41
